  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Win it back – seven seconds to finish",
  "description": "Played in the last third of a 9v9 pitch. Equal numbers in both teams, but red also has a goalkeeper. Both teams line up in their formation, and all players stay in the third.\n\nRed's goalkeeper starts by playing the ball to blue, who must keep it within the team. If blue loses the ball they must win it back at once – and then have seven seconds to get a shot away. After winning the ball, red must make five passes within the team and then take the ball out of the third, by dribbling over the line or passing to a player running in behind.\n\nProgression: move the game to the middle third. Blue then counters into the last third after winning the ball, and the goalkeeper may intercept long passes. The diagram shows only the last third and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "When you lose the ball: the nearest player presses at once, the others close the passes around the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "After winning it back – look for the way to goal straight away, seven seconds go fast."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep players close to the ball when you attack, so you are close when it is lost."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Red: play the first pass out of pressure, then find width and depth."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
